<h2>Jenny</h2>

<p>Jenny is a Registered Yoga Teacher (RYT) with Yoga Alliance, bringing over a decade of dedicated experience in yoga practice and teaching, with particular expertise in Therapeutic Yoga and Restorative Yoga. She has been teaching Yoga at UNI Yoga Academy at senior tutor level in Vietnam, leading and contributing to numerous 200-hour and 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training programmes, mentoring and supporting the next generation of Yoga teachers. Restorative Yoga is a core component of her curriculum, reflecting her commitment to practices that support deep healing and recovery.</p>

<p>In recent years, Jenny has expanded her practice into Sound Healing, completing extensive training in therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation. She integrates meridian sound healing, therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation into her classes to support deep relaxation, energetic balance and holistic healing.</p>

<p>Known for her calm presence and authentic approach, Jenny creates a grounded and supportive space where students can slow down, reconnect with their bodies and cultivate deeper awareness. Her work bridges traditional yogic wisdom with therapeutic practice, and her understanding of how sound, breath and movement interact along the body's energy pathways informs every class she teaches. Jenny and Seb also offer joint sessions combining Qigong and Sound Healing, and within the online Qigong courses Jenny teaches Qigong alongside Seb and takes on selected elements of the TCM and practice curriculum.</p>

<p>Beyond her practice and teaching, Jenny is an initiate in the Inchegiri Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>

