<h2>Seb</h2>

<p>Seb brings over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. His path began with Yoga in 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India while remaining committed to its authentic roots beyond modern trends. He is a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea, and continues to draw on the depth of that long practice in his teaching today.</p>

<p>In 2010 he turned his focus to authentic Qigong, training extensively with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. What started as a personal practice quickly became a vocation. Seb went on to lead Qigong groups in Tokyo, Vienna and Seoul, sharing these practices with diverse communities and deepening his understanding of Qi cultivation and the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work and the body's meridian system.</p>

<p>In parallel with his Qigong training, Seb qualified as a Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, and holds a certificate in Advanced TCM Reflexology. This gave him a precise, hands-on framework for working directly with the body's energy lines. He has taught at senior tutor level at the Traditional Thai Massage Association Japan and at the Shivaga Traditional Medical School in Japan, where he delivered Therapeutic Thai Bodywork, Reflexology and Qigong.</p>

<p>When Seb began working with Jenny, the combination of Qigong and Sound Healing emerged naturally from the complementary nature of their training. His background in Qi cultivation, energy work and therapeutic bodywork paired with Jenny's expertise in Therapeutic Yoga and Sound Healing, and their joint sessions now combine both practices into a single guided experience.</p>

<p>On a note unrelated to any mundane practices and considerations, Seb is an initiate and direct disciple in the Inchegiri Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>

